// The unsafe neighbour of lifetime_mix_flow_inner_borrow_used_inside: the
// variable still holds the inner local's borrow when it is used after the
// block, where that local is gone.
//
// Verdict: refuse, ErrorFrozen at the inner local, which goes out of scope
// while 'r' still holds a borrow of it (ref_flow_freeze's "goes out of scope
// while" idiom). Under the flow rule the store 'r = &y' is legal; what is
// refused is keeping it past 'y''s end.
// Basis: language rule (2 Oct 2026), the flow rule -- a variable's lifetime
// follows what it currently holds; refborref.html, "Lifetime Constraints".
// Rust refuses it (E0597, "'y' does not live long enough"; by reading, not
// run). Where the diagnostic lands is a reading of the rules above.
// Master d331baab: refused, but at the store 'r = &y' with ErrorInvType,
// which the flow rule makes legal. Stage 4 fixed it.

mod lifetime_mix_flow_inner_borrow_used_after;

fn f(p &i64) i64 {
  mut r = p;
  {
    imm y = 1i64;            //~ ErrorFrozen
    r = &y;
  }
  *r;
}
